      </species>
      <species id="mw43cbf288_04b6_4831_be11_4fd49093a2b2" name="qPSC" compartment="mw6d681743_210d_45e7_b5cb_ea5176345395" initialAmount="0" substanceUnits="MWUSERUNIT_cell" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="true" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Quiescent pancreatic stellate cells in tumor compartment. In normal pancreas, PSCs store vitamin A and maintain stromal homeostasis.</body>
        </notes>
      </species>
      <species id="mwef278930_37c4_4794_a034_e539049713ad" name="iCAF" compartment="mw6d681743_210d_45e7_b5cb_ea5176345395" initialAmount="0" substanceUnits="MWUSERUNIT_cell" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="true" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Inflammatory cancer-associated fibroblasts. Secrete IL-6 and CXCL12, driving MDSC recruitment, M2 polarization, and CXCR4-mediated T-cell exclusion (Elyada 2019, Ogawa 2021). Driven by tumor-derived IL-1alpha; TGFb antagonizes via IL-1R1 repression.</body>
        </notes>
      </species>
      <species id="mwa75a976b_7300_45cc_900c_5003a74286b4" name="myCAF" compartment="mw6d681743_210d_45e7_b5cb_ea5176345395" initialAmount="0" substanceUnits="MWUSERUNIT_cell" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="true" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Myofibroblastic cancer-associated fibroblasts. Secrete ECM (collagen), TGFb, VEGF. Build desmoplastic barrier. Favored by TGFb signaling (Biffi 2019). (CXCL12 is iCAF-derived, not myCAF -- audit m2-A-ECM-01.)</body>
        </notes>
      </species>
      <species id="mw7b1b4278_9d57_4db8_a9e1_f3af70ff4348" name="apCAF" compartment="mw6d681743_210d_45e7_b5cb_ea5176345395" initialAmount="0" substanceUnits="MWUSERUNIT_cell" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="true" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Antigen-presenting cancer-associated fibroblasts. Express MHC-II, present tumor antigen tolerogenically -&gt; Treg induction. Rarest subtype ~2-5% of CAFs (Elyada 2019).</body>
        </notes>
      </species>
      <species id="mwd545f401_5e54_4823_8038_313e32ea9746" name="collagen" compartment="mw6d681743_210d_45e7_b5cb_ea5176345395" initialAmount="0" substanceUnits="MWBUILTINPREFIX_milli_MWBUILTINUNIT_gram" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="true" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Fibrillar collagen (types I/III) in tumor (total mass in mg). Primary structural ECM component driving desmoplasia. Determines pore size (immune exclusion) and stiffness (mechanotransduction).</body>
        </notes>
      </species>
      <species id="mw73b595fe_3c9b_41d8_85e2_e0b2ab6ffb7c" name="CXCL12" compartment="mw6d681743_210d_45e7_b5cb_ea5176345395" initialConcentration="0" substanceUnits="MWDERIVEDUNIT_nanomolarity_milliliter" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="false" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">CXCL12/SDF-1 chemokine secreted by iCAFs. Major T cell exclusion mechanism in PDAC via CXCR4 signaling (Elyada 2019, Ogawa 2021).</body>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <SimBiology xmlns="http://www.mathworks.com">
            <Unit Numerator="nanomolarity"/>
          </SimBiology>
        </annotation>
      </species>
      <species id="mwb96b4e09_51da_48dc_aec7_1fb16ede2b2b" name="IL6" compartment="mw6d681743_210d_45e7_b5cb_ea5176345395" initialConcentration="0" substanceUnits="MWDERIVEDUNIT_nanomolarity_milliliter" hasOnlySubstanceUnits="false" boundaryCondition="false" constant="false">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Interleukin-6 inflammatory cytokine secreted by iCAFs. Promotes MDSC recruitment, M2 polarization, tumor progression.</body>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <SimBiology xmlns="http://www.mathworks.com">
            <Unit Numerator="nanomolarity"/>
          </SimBiology>
        </annotation>
